# Directories Bazel must not descend into when resolving a target pattern like //...
#
# e2e is a separate Bazel module with its own MODULE.bazel, .bazelrc and .bazelversion: it is the
# end-to-end workspace, built by running bazel inside it, and its packages are deliberately not
# part of this module's target universe.
#
# Without this entry `bazel query //...` fails. Running bazel inside e2e/ leaves bazel-bin,
# bazel-out and bazel-e2e convenience symlinks that point into the output base. .gitignore covers
# them with `bazel-*`, but Bazel does not read .gitignore: the outer workspace follows those
# symlinks into the output base, finds the external repositories checked out there and tries to
# load packages from them, failing with an unresolvable repo such as `@rules_shellcheck`. The
# error names an external repo and a tests/runfiles path, neither of which is in this source
# tree, so it looks like a dependency problem when the cause is directory traversal.
e2e
